<title>USA: Koch raises U.S. posted crude prices 50 cents.</title>
<headline>Koch raises U.S. posted crude prices 50 cents.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil Co, a division of Koch Industries, said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents, effective Wednesday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $17.50 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $14.75 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $17.00 and Oklahoma sweet is $17.50.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
